{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-cancel-order","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL injection vulnerability in order cancellation reason parameter","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/orders.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":50,"end_line":52},"explanation":"In `cancel_order`, the `reason` taken from the JSON request body is formatted directly into the SQL UPDATE string (`f\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = '{reason}' WHERE id = ?\"`). An attacker can supply a malicious string containing SQL syntax to execute arbitrary SQL commands or extract data from the database.","suggested_fix":"Use parameterized queries for `cancel_reason`, e.g., `db.execute(\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = ? WHERE id = ?\", (reason, int(order_id)))`.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O1","note":"The cancellation reason is interpolated directly into the SQL query string via f-string instead of using parameterized queries.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/orders.py","start_line":50,"end_line":52,"snippet":"    reason = request.json().get(\"reason\", \"\")\n    sql = f\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = '{reason}' WHERE id = ?\"\n    db.execute(sql, (int(order_id),))","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":11874,"output_tokens":326,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":2014},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":3,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":3,"tool_calls":2,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":26.27,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-cancel-order","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL injection vulnerability in cancel_order via unescaped reason field formatted directly into the SQL query string","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/orders.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":51,"end_line":51},"explanation":"The `reason` string from the request JSON is interpolated directly into the SQL update query via an f-string instead of using parameterized queries. An attacker can supply a malicious string containing SQL commands to execute arbitrary SQL statements against the database.","suggested_fix":"Use parameterized query: db.execute(\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = ? WHERE id = ?\", (reason, int(order_id)))","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O1","note":"reason is interpolated directly into the SQL string via f-string","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/orders.py","start_line":51,"end_line":51,"snippet":"    sql = f\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = '{reason}' WHERE id = ?\"","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O1","note":"sql string containing user input is executed directly via db.execute","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/orders.py","start_line":52,"end_line":52,"snippet":"    db.execute(sql, (int(order_id),))","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":11693,"output_tokens":351,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":2013},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":3,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":3,"tool_calls":2,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":24.306,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-set-role","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Updating a non-existent user's role does not return 404 or check if the update affected any rows, unlike other admin endpoints.","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/admin.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":28,"end_line":38},"explanation":"When an admin attempts to change the role of a non-existent user id, `set_role` updates 0 rows silently and succeeds with 204 (or raises a TypeError if notify is True because `get_user` returns `None` and accessing `user.email` raises `AttributeError`). It should check if the user exists or if any rows were changed and raise a 404 error, similar to `deactivate_user`.","suggested_fix":"Check if the user exists or if `db.execute(...) == 0` and raise `HTTPError(404, \"user not found\")`.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O2","note":"set_role executes UPDATE without checking if any rows were updated, and calls get_user which can return None when notify is True","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/admin.py","start_line":28,"end_line":38,"snippet":"@router.post(\"/users/{user_id}/role\")\ndef set_role(request: Request, user_id: str) -> Response:\n    payload = request.json()\n    role = payload[\"role\"]\n    notify = payload.get(\"notify\", True)\n    db.execute(\"UPDATE users SET role = ? WHERE id = ?\", (role, int(user_id)))\n    if not notify:\n        return Response(status=204)\n    user = get_user(db, int(user_id))\n    send_email(user.email, \"Your role has changed\", f\"You are now {role}.\")\n    return Response(status=204)","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O6","note":"deactivate_user correctly checks if changed == 0 and raises HTTPError 404","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/admin.py","start_line":20,"end_line":24,"snippet":"@router.post(\"/users/{user_id}/deactivate\")\ndef deactivate_user(request: Request, user_id: str) -> Response:\n    changed = db.execute(\"UPDATE users SET active = 0 WHERE id = ?\", (int(user_id),))\n    if changed == 0:\n        raise HTTPError(404, \"user not found\")","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O3","note":"get_user returns None if the user does not exist","ref":"head","path":"app/users.py","start_line":9,"end_line":13,"snippet":"def get_user(db: Database, user_id: int) -> User | None:\n    \"\"\"Return the user, or None if no such user exists.\"\"\"\n    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT id, email, role, active FROM users WHERE id = ?\", (user_id,))\n    if row is None:\n        return None","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"none-user","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":14994,"output_tokens":541,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":4,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":4,"tool_calls":3,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":46.43,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-set-role","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Updating the role of a non-existent user results in a 500 error or a sent email to None instead of a 404 response.","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/admin.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":33,"end_line":37},"explanation":"In `set_role`, if `user_id` does not exist in the database, `db.execute` performs an update that affects 0 rows, but does not raise or return 404 (unlike `deactivate_user` which checks `changed == 0`). Then, if `notify` is true (the default), `get_user` returns `None`, and accessing `user.email` raises an `AttributeError` (or fails when sending email), causing a 500 Internal Server Error instead of returning a 404 Not Found status.","suggested_fix":"Check if any row was changed or if the user exists, and raise HTTPError(404, \"user not found\") like deactivate_user does.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O3","note":"If user_id does not exist, db.execute updates 0 rows, then get_user returns None, and user.email raises an AttributeError (or TypeError if send_email handles it/fails).","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/admin.py","start_line":33,"end_line":37,"snippet":"    db.execute(\"UPDATE users SET role = ? WHERE id = ?\", (role, int(user_id)))\n    if not notify:\n        return Response(status=204)\n    user = get_user(db, int(user_id))\n    send_email(user.email, \"Your role has changed\", f\"You are now {role}.\")","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O8","note":"get_user returns None if the user does not exist in the database.","ref":"head","path":"app/users.py","start_line":9,"end_line":13,"snippet":"def get_user(db: Database, user_id: int) -> User | None:\n    \"\"\"Return the user, or None if no such user exists.\"\"\"\n    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT id, email, role, active FROM users WHERE id = ?\", (user_id,))\n    if row is None:\n        return None","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"none-user","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":20686,"output_tokens":546,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":5,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":5,"tool_calls":4,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":119.441,"error":null}
