{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-number-converter-rename","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"The pull request renames the `signed` parameter to `allow_negative` in `NumberConverter` and `FloatConverter`, but leaves references to `signed` in the docstrings and example snippets of `IntegerConverter` and `FloatConverter`.","category":"correctness","severity":"low","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":183,"end_line":184},"explanation":"The pull request updates the keyword parameter name from `signed` to `allow_negative`, but leaves parts of the docstrings for `IntegerConverter` and `FloatConverter` referring to the `signed` parameter, which is inconsistent and misleading for users reading the documentation.","suggested_fix":"Update the docstring descriptions in IntegerConverter and FloatConverter to refer to the allow_negative parameter.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O38","note":"Docstring still mentions the signed parameter instead of allow_negative","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","start_line":183,"end_line":184,"snippet":"    By default it only accepts unsigned, positive values. The ``signed``\n    parameter will enable signed, negative values. ::","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O40","note":"Docstring still mentions the signed parameter instead of allow_negative","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","start_line":208,"end_line":209,"snippet":"    By default it only accepts unsigned, positive values. The ``signed``\n    parameter will enable signed, negative values. ::","query":null}]}],"matches":[],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":44590,"output_tokens":931,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":24246},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":7,"cached_requests"